course: dictionary
lesson: 13801
title: Words that describe how things happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Invisibly comes from invisible, which means you cannot see it. Add -ly and it tells you how something happens: in a way that cannot be seen.
explain: «The ghost drifted invisibly through the old wall.» You cannot see the ghost move, so invisibly tells you how it moved. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Try "in a way nobody can see" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Invisibly can also mean without people noticing. «The helpers cleaned the hall invisibly before anyone arrived.» Nobody saw them working, so they did their job quietly in the background.
fact: Invisibly is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Invisibly» means in a way that cannot be seen.
fact: «Invisibly» can also mean without people noticing, quietly in the background.
fact: Air moves invisibly, so you can feel the wind but you cannot see the air itself.
fact: Germs spread invisibly because they are too small to see.
exercise: «The spy moved invisibly through the crowd.» What does invisibly mean here? | Slowly, one step at a time | In a way that people can see clearly | *In a way that cannot be seen | Very loudly, with a big band
exercise: «The helpers worked invisibly, and the classroom was always tidy by morning.» Find and copy the word that tells how the helpers worked. | classroom | helpers | morning | *invisibly
exercise: Mum says, «Germs spread invisibly on our hands.» What does she mean? | *They spread in a way we cannot see, because they are too small | They spread only in summer | They spread in a way we cannot see | They spread loudly through the house
test: «The ghost drifted invisibly through the old wall.» What does invisibly mean in this sentence? | Happily | Very fast | *In a way that cannot be seen | Very loudly
test: Sam says, «The helpers cleaned the hall invisibly.» What does Sam mean? | They cleaned very loudly | *They did it without anyone noticing them | They cleaned the hall with bright paint | They cleaned the hall in the dark
exam: «Air moves invisibly around us.» What is the best meaning of invisibly here? | Under the sea | Very fast | Loudly | *In a way that cannot be seen
